# Config screen tooltips (parallel budget + chain preview appearance)
config.qz_miner.parallelBudgetMode.tooltip=Parallel budget mode: deadline shares the tickBudgetMs soft deadline (default, same as before); slice uses a per-tick slice budget so the main thread no longer waits for the full deadline
config.qz_miner.parallelSliceBudgetMs.tooltip=Per-tick parallel slice budget in milliseconds for slice mode (1..40); ignored in deadline mode
config.qz_miner.clientPreviewRenderBackend.tooltip=Preview render backend: auto uses shader when capability detection passes, otherwise legacy (default); explicit shader still falls back to legacy and records a diagnostic; legacy always uses the fixed pipeline
config.qz_miner.clientPreviewBarThickness.tooltip=Preview bar thickness (block-space offset scale), default 0.045, range 0.005..0.2
config.qz_miner.clientPreviewColorSource.tooltip=Preview color source: builtin constant color (default, byte-for-byte identical to before); config uses the four RGB keys below for semantic colors
config.qz_miner.clientPreviewColorPrimary.tooltip=Primary local prediction color (#RRGGBB, 0xRRGGBB or decimal), default 0x40E6FF
config.qz_miner.clientPreviewColorSecondary.tooltip=Sub-mode local prediction color (#RRGGBB, 0xRRGGBB or decimal), default 0x40E6FF
config.qz_miner.clientPreviewColorRemote.tooltip=Remote predicted color (#RRGGBB, 0xRRGGBB or decimal), default 0x40E6FF
config.qz_miner.clientPreviewColorTruncated.tooltip=Truncated target color (#RRGGBB, 0xRRGGBB or decimal), default 0x40E6FF
config.qz_miner.clientPreviewDepthMode.tooltip=Depth channel: xray is always visible (default, same as before); occlude uses depth testing; outline adds a body pass plus a top-most outline pass
config.qz_miner.clientPreviewAnimation.tooltip=Preview animation: off disables animation (default, current baseline); flow grows uniformly; wave grows wave by wave in appearance order (wired in a later batch)
config.qz_miner.clientPreviewAnimationDurationMs.tooltip=Animation duration per generation in milliseconds; 0 completes instantly; range 0..2000
config.qz_miner.clientPreviewAnimationPhase.tooltip=Animation phase source: order uses the appearance index (default); hash uses a stable coordinate + generation hash. Reserved, not wired this round: rendering reads only the animation id and duration, so changing this key has no visual effect; appearance order is carried by animation=wave, and the hash phase is deferred
config.qz_miner.clientPreviewFadeMode.tooltip=Distance fade refresh: timer keeps the historical 1 Hz fallback (default, same as before); signal is driven by camera change signals (wired in a later batch); gpu computes the fade per frame in the shader
config.qz_miner.clientPreviewFadeRefreshDistance.tooltip=Camera movement threshold in blocks for signal mode; the visual revision advances once reached; range 0..8
config.qz_miner.clientPreviewFadeFallbackMs.tooltip=Fallback refresh interval in milliseconds for signal mode without camera movement; range 50..5000
config.qz_miner.clientPreviewMinScreenWidthPx.tooltip=Minimum on-screen bar width in pixels; 0 disables clamping (default, same as before) and 1..8 takes effect, keeping distant bars at least that wide on screen; range 0..8
config.qz_miner.clientPreviewOutlineWidthPx.tooltip=Outline shell expansion along the face direction in physical pixels; default 1.5 (unchanged look, previously a hard-coded value in the renderer), 0 disables the outline; range 0..8; only the shader backend draws the outline shell in outline depth mode
config.qz_miner.clientPreviewFaceShading.tooltip=Bake view-independent face shading (top brightest, bottom darkest); default false (bit-identical to the pre-wiring look). When enabled, the legacy color stream and the shader vertex color use the same brightness table (literal constant x the same palette constant, bit-identical)
config.qz_miner.clientPreviewTruncationSignal.tooltip=Whether a preview truncated by the target cap is shown visibly; default false (HUD display wired in a later batch)
config.qz_miner.clientPreviewMaxTargetsHardCap.tooltip=Hard cap on preview targets, range 1..4096; the effective value is the smallest of this, clientPreviewMaxTargets and the server chainMaxBlocks
config.qz_miner.clientPreviewLod.tooltip=LOD for extreme scales: off disables it (default, same as before); auto merges by distance and culls by alpha
config.qz_miner.clientPreviewLodMinAlpha.tooltip=LOD alpha cull threshold; bars below it are not built; range 0..1
config.qz_miner.clientPreviewOrderMinBrightness.tooltip=Lower bound of the chain-order brightness weight; color brightness falls linearly with a bar's appearance index (farther from the aimed origin means a larger index) while alpha is left untouched, so distance fade stays authoritative on its own. Range 0..1; 1.0 disables the feature (same as before) and the default 0.55 keeps the origin at 1.0 and the farthest bar at 0.55; shader backend only
config.qz_miner.clientPreviewSuppressVanillaHighlight.tooltip=Suppress the vanilla block highlight when the preview is active on the same target, avoiding a double indicator
config.qz_miner.clientPreviewVersionedInputs.tooltip=Whether to use the versioned preview input snapshot (including target debounce); default false (wired in a later batch); when disabled the per-field comparison path is used
config.qz_miner.clientPreviewPresentationOverlay.tooltip=Whether to enable the unified presentation projection overlay (single source of truth for HUD truncation, progress and remote failures)
config.qz_miner.clientPreviewExecutionProgress.tooltip=Whether the HUD shows execution progress (executed / matched); the progress comes from client-side world sampling (no protocol change, easy to revert), default off. Only destroyed targets (block turned to air) are counted; interaction and replacement targets are not
config.qz_miner.clientPreviewBackendDiagnostics.tooltip=Whether the HUD shows preview backend diagnostics (active backend id and the one-shot fallback reason); the data comes from the backend state snapshot published by the render thread. Off by default.
config.qz_miner.clientPreviewRemoteTimeoutMs.tooltip=Remote preview request timeout in milliseconds, range 250..60000; on timeout stale responses are dropped and preview activation is cleared

